{
  "message": "I can help troubleshoot mobile data issues. Since you’re abroad in France and don’t have Wi‑Fi, I’ll need to look up the line first so I can check relevant account/line details and data usage. Please provide the mobile phone number for the affected line.",
  "sources": [
    "telecom/main_policy.md:telecom-agent-policy",
    "telecom/tech_support_workflow.md:phone-device---technical-support-troubleshooting-workflow-1de605819f70"
  ]
}

{
  "message": "I found the affected line 555-123-2002, and it is Active. I also see international roaming is currently disabled on that line. Since you’re abroad in France, mobile data may not work properly unless roaming is enabled. Would you like me to enable international roaming for this line?",
  "sources": [
    "telecom/tech_support_workflow.md:phone-device---technical-support-troubleshooting-workflow-4eb676efe9f0"
  ]
}

{
  "message": "International roaming has been enabled for line 555-123-2002. Please check your mobile data connection now. If it is still slow or stops completely, we can continue troubleshooting by checking data usage and other network settings.",
  "sources": [
    "telecom/tech_support_workflow.md:phone-device---technical-support-troubleshooting-workflow-4eb676efe9f0"
  ]
}

{
  "message": "Your current billing-cycle data usage for line 555-123-2002 is 15.1 GB, and the data limit is 15.0 GB, so the data limit has been exceeded. When data usage is exceeded, the troubleshooting workflow says to ask whether you want to change to another plan or refuel data. I can help refuel data for this line if you’d like. After refueling, you should rerun the speed test and check data connectivity.",
  "sources": [
    "telecom/tech_support_workflow.md:phone-device---technical-support-troubleshooting-workflow-1de605819f70"
  ]
}

{
  "message": "Successfully added 2.0 GB of data to line 555-123-2002. The charge is $4.00. Please rerun the speed test and check your mobile data connectivity now. If there is still no connectivity, the troubleshooting workflow says we should transfer you to technical support.",
  "sources": [
    "telecom/tech_support_workflow.md:phone-device---technical-support-troubleshooting-workflow-1de605819f70"
  ]
}

{
  "message": "YOU ARE BEING TRANSFERRED TO A HUMAN AGENT. PLEASE HOLD."
}

{
  "message": "I can help troubleshoot the cellular “No Service” issue. Please provide the phone number for the affected line so I can look up the line and start checking its status. Source: telecom/main_policy.md:telecom-agent-policy"
}

{
  "message": "I found the affected line ending in 2002. The line status is Active, so it does not appear to be suspended. To continue troubleshooting “No Service,” please check your phone’s status bar and network status. Specifically, tell me: whether Airplane Mode is on, the signal strength shown, the network type if any, whether mobile data is enabled, and whether the SIM shows any error. These are standard diagnostic checks for cellular connection issues. Sources: telecom/main_policy.md:telecom-agent-policy, telecom/tech_support_workflow.md:phone-device---technical-support-troubleshooting-workflow-fbe139dd2bc1"
}

{
  "message": "Please check the Status Bar first and tell me what icons you see for cellular signal, mobile data, Wi-Fi, and battery. Source: telecom/tech_support_workflow.md:phone-device---technical-support-troubleshooting-workflow-fbe139dd2bc1"
}

{
  "message": "Next, please check Network Status and tell me whether Airplane Mode is on or off, the signal strength, network type if any, whether mobile data is enabled, and whether data roaming is enabled. Source: telecom/tech_support_workflow.md:phone-device---technical-support-troubleshooting-workflow-fbe139dd2bc1"
}

{
  "message": "YOU ARE BEING TRANSFERRED TO A HUMAN AGENT. PLEASE HOLD."
}

{"message":"Yes. Please turn mobile data back on, then run a speed test and check whether mobile data connectivity is working.

The available troubleshooting actions include toggling mobile data, and the workflow says that after refueling data, you should rerun a speed test and check data connectivity. Source: telecom/tech_support_workflow.md:phone-device---technical-support-troubleshooting-workflow-4eb676efe9f0 and telecom/tech_support_workflow.md:phone-device---technical-support-troubleshooting-workflow-1de605819f70

If it still does not work after mobile data is on, tell me the result."}

{"message":"Turn off Data Saver first, then run the speed test and check mobile data connectivity.

Data Saver is an available setting that controls data-saving behavior, and the workflow asks you to rerun a speed test and check connectivity after the data/roaming fixes. Source: telecom/tech_support_workflow.md:phone-device---technical-support-troubleshooting-workflow-4eb676efe9f0 and telecom/tech_support_workflow.md:phone-device---technical-support-troubleshooting-workflow-1de605819f70

If the speed or connectivity is still poor after Data Saver is off, tell me the result."}

{"message":"Yes, please run the speed test now and check whether mobile data connectivity is working.

The troubleshooting workflow says that after addressing exceeded data usage by refueling data, you should rerun the speed test and check data connectivity. Source: telecom/tech_support_workflow.md:phone-device---technical-support-troubleshooting-workflow-1de605819f70

If there is still no connectivity or it remains unusably slow, tell me the result."}

{"message":"Yes — we can try simpler, read-only checks first.

Please check the phone’s **SIM status** if you can. The SIM status check is meant to show whether the SIM card is working correctly and its current status [telecom/tech_support_workflow.md:phone-device---technical-support-troubleshooting-workflow-fbe139dd2bc1].

If you can’t find SIM status or don’t feel comfortable looking for it, that’s okay. Since the line is active and Airplane Mode didn’t fix the signal, I can transfer you to a human technical support agent for more help."}

{"message":"The SIM status check is meant to show whether the SIM card is working correctly, and “no SIM card detected” indicates the phone is not detecting the SIM [telecom/tech_support_workflow.md:phone-device---technical-support-troubleshooting-workflow-fbe139dd2bc1].

The supported next fix is to reseat the SIM card, which means removing and reinserting it; this can help resolve recognition issues [telecom/tech_support_workflow.md:phone-device---technical-support-troubleshooting-workflow-4eb676efe9f0].

Since you said you’re not comfortable doing that, I can transfer you to a human technical support agent for help with the SIM issue. Would you like me to transfer you?"}

{"message":"Your line has used 15.1 GB of a 15.0 GB limit, so your data usage is exceeded. The current cycle ends on 2025-02-28.

Per the mobile-data troubleshooting workflow, when data usage is exceeded, I should ask whether you want to change plan or refuel data, then have you rerun a speed test and check data connectivity after that. [telecom/tech_support_workflow.md:phone-device---technical-support-troubleshooting-workflow-1de605819f70]

Would you like to refuel data on this line? If yes, tell me how many GB you want to add."}
